<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia cuts April crude palm oil export tax.</title>
<headline>Indonesia cuts April crude palm oil export tax.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia cut its export tax on crude palm oil to $41.08 a tonne in April from $52.52 in March, the Finance Ministry said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The tax on palm olein was reduced to $54.60 a tonne in April from $65.10 in March, while that on RBD palm oil was lowered to $43.68 in April from $55.64.</p>
<p>The tax on crude olein was reduced to $58.10 a tonne in April from $63.70 in March.</p>
<p>The export taxes, introduced in September 1994, are based on a composite average of international prices in the last two weeks of the previous month and are aimed at ensuring sufficient supply and stable prices in the domestic market.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
